  cybersecurity, digital modernization, and
  integrated systems.
  Leidos operates through four main divisions:
  • Defense & Intelligence: Cybersecurity,
  signals intelligence, and mission support.
  • Civil: IT infrastructure, energy engineering,
  and transportation security.
  • Health: Healthcare data management and
  medical enterprise optimization.
  • Advanced Solutions: Research, space, and
  emerging technologies.
  The company has faced scrutiny, including a
  2025 termination of a $2.4 billion DHS
  cybersecurity contract for convenience, a
  Chinese export ban on dual-use goods, and
  ongoing DOJ investigations into potential
  foreign bribery and antitrust issues related to
  2021-2022 contracts.
  Financials
  Leidos maintains solid financial performance,
